WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.160
True crime is the most investigated and

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.800
indicted genre of the night.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.520
So let's hear from the
main parties summoned.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:15.000
Starting with The Staircase, with witnesses
Colin Firth and Toni Collette, the

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.040
series has more twists than a
long staircase, leading us to the

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.979
question: accident or murder?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.360
Does the outrageous amount of blood
at the crime scene fit a simple fall

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.800
down the stairs? I assure you, Your
Honor, it was the opposite amount of blood

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.479
to what Elizabeth Holmes, in The Dropout,
meant to draw from patients with her

00:00:38.519 --> 00:00:40.960
revolutionary Theranos machine.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.559
A single drop. The system promised
a full blood test from just

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.280
one drop of human blood.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.320
Million-dollar tech, built
on millions of lies, right?

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.920
Since the so-called
technology didn't even exist.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.440
And speaking of con artists, we
have to talk about Inventing Anna.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.600
Anna Delvey posed as an eccentric
millionaire and fully infiltrated

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.960
New York high society.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.600
All smooth talk, tiptoeing in Louboutins
and promising a wire transfer,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.960
a Venmo for the people.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.100
Also summoned to the 2022 Emmys was Only
Murders in the Building, which tells the

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.720
story of 3 true crime buffs
who end up caught up in one.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.000
Though I must say in my closing
arguments, Your Honor, that the biggest

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.440
crime of the Emmys was leaving
Selena out of the night's subpoenas.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.700
Case closed.
